        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="200" start="579" end="580.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy and Darius hear a knock on the door.  They both look toward the sound.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="201" start="580.64001" end="582.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy looks up from his video game.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="202" start="582.12" end="582.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The door opens. Earn is standing outside.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="203" start="582.71997" end="587.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn makes a joke.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">A gun sticks out from the door, pointed directly at Earn's head. Earn comments on their peep hole.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="204" start="587.64001" end="590.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy looks through the cracked door, recognizes Earn, withdraws gun, and shuts the door to unlock it.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="205" start="590.88" end="596.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Paper Boy Alfred and Darius are concerned about security and ready to fight.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius hides behind a wall, wearing an apron and a kitchen towel over his face. He's holding a large kitchen knife and a plate of cookies. Alfred Paper Boy and Earn walk into the room and Alfred Paper Boy points to Darius to introduce him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="206" start="596.76001" end="598.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius pulls the towel off of his face and offers Earn a cookie.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="207" start="598.88" end="601.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn thinks Darius is strange.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn takes a cookie, thanks Darius, and follows Alfred Paper Boy into the house.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="208" start="601.52002" end="604.79999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn walks into the room and starts to make small talk.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="209" start="604.79999" end="606.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy cuts right to the chase.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy cuts Earn off and accuses him of wanting to get in on his fame.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="210" start="606.12" end="608.32001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn feigns surprise at being called out.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn laughs and denies wanting to get in on Alfred Paper Boy's fame.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="211" start="608.32001" end="609.15997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy starts to reply to Earn.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="212" start="609.15997" end="613.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy does not believe Earn.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy says that people are only nice when they want something.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="213" start="613.23999" end="614.08002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is referring to Lottie, his daughter.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn replies that he was nice to a girl this morning.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="214" start="614.08002" end="616">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred paper Boy replies that talking about his daughter is gross.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="215" start="616" end="618.08002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn tries to make a joke.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn says it would be gross if he was trying to have sex with his daughter. Darius stands and eats cookies in the background.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="216" start="618.08002" end="620.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">No one laughs at Earn's joke. Alfred Paper Boy sighs and stands.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="217" start="620.35999" end="624.15997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy and Darius sit down on couches. Earn tells Alfred Paper Boy he wants to manage him. Alfred Paper Boy laughs.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="218" start="624.15997" end="626.32001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy does not take Earn seriously.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy starts rolling weed (marijuana) into a blunt. He asks Earn if he knows where the word manage comes from.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="219" start="626.32001" end="628.20001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn sits on the arm of the sofa and correctly responds that manus comes from the Latin word for hand. Darius eats a cookie on the couch behind him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="220" start="628.20001" end="635.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy continues rolling the blunt (marijuana cigar). He says Earn is probably right, but the point he's trying to make is that you have to be a man to manage, and Earn is not man enough.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="221" start="635.12" end="635.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn questions what Alfred Paper Boy means about being a man not being his lane.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="222" start="635.88" end="636.91998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is referring to Malcolm X, and means he wants someone tough and aggressive.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy says he needs a manager who is like Malcolm.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="223" start="636.91998" end="640">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy sees Earn as more gentle and reserved, like Martin Luther King Jr. He thinks gentle, reserved people get killed in his line of work.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy sits back and rolls the blunt (marijuana cigar) between his fingers. He says Earn is too much like Martin. He then says that they killed Martin.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="224" start="640" end="641.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn questions Alfred Paper Boy's logic, since both men he referenced were killed. Darius sits on the couch behind him. Darius sits in the background saying a blessing over his plate of cookies.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="225" start="641.23999" end="645.08002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius speaks up from the background, claiming that no one knows if Malcolm X is dead because no one has seen his body since his funeral.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="226" start="645.08002" end="652">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn responds to Darius, turns back to Alfred Paper Boy and tries to convince him he'd make a good manager.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="227" start="652" end="654.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn continues trying to convince Alfred Paper Boy he would be a good manager. Alfred Paper Boy licks the blunt (marijuana cigar) and looks up and Earn.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="228" start="654.35999" end="655.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn continues trying to convince Alfred Paper Boy he would make a good manager.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="229" start="655.76001" end="656.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius compares Earn to Don Lemon.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="230" start="656.88" end="660.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Darius is an odd, but sometimes randomly insightful person</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn realizes Darius actually made a good point and begins to rephrase his argument</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="231" start="660.56" end="662.03998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Darius realizes they missed four twenty, a ceremonial time of day for them to smoke</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius cuts Earn off, suddenly realizing it is four thirty</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="232" start="662.03998" end="663.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy and Darius were trying to be ready to smoke at four twenty, but missed it</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy looks at his watch and realizes they are late</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="233" start="663.52002" end="668.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Outside, Alfred Paper Boy lights the blunt (marijuana cigar) in his mouth, pulls on it, and sits back.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="234" start="668.71997" end="672.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, and Darius sit on a couch on the grass across from Alfred Paper Boy's house, smoking a blunt (marijuana cigar).</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="235" start="672.56" end="673.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, and Darius sit on the couch in the grass. Alfred Paper Boy offers Earn the blunt (marijuana cigar) and Earn turns it down.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="236" start="673.64001" end="675">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is surprised Earn turned down the blunt (marijuana cigar).</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy, still offering the blunt (marijuana cigar) to Earn, asks him when he stopped smoking weed (marijuana).</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="237" start="675" end="676.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn says he doesn't want to smoke marijuana and get high while doing business.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="238" start="676.23999" end="679.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Darius is surprised and confused</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The three characters are sitting on the couch in the grass. Alfred Paper Boy retracts his arm with the blunt (marijuana cigar). Darius questions whether Earn can manage a rapper if he won't smoke marijuana while doing business</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="239" start="679.23999" end="685.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">The double meaning in Darius's comment is that Earn should find a child's or amateur's job if he can't get high and do business.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy takes another pull from the blunt (marijuana cigar). Darius says that VH1 is hiring interns, which sounds like a joke, but he saw it on Twitter this morning.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="240" start="685.76001" end="687.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn silently looks at Darius and slowly turns away</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="241" start="687.88" end="691.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy takes another hit of the blunt (marijuana cigar) and passes it to Darius. He asks Earn how Princeton is going.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="242" start="691.64001" end="696.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy knows Earn is keeping a secret about his time in college and is questioning it</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius takes a hit of the blunt (marijuana cigar). Alfred Paper Boy asks Earn if he's still taking a year off from Princeton, because he has not returned for three years now</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="243" start="696.35999" end="697.40002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn doesn't answer the implied question.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn replies shortly</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="244" start="697.40002" end="699.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is digging for information on why Earn left school</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy says he knows why Earn has not gone back to college at Princeton</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="245" start="699.56" end="701.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn does not want to discuss school and why he left</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn cuts him off and replies firmly that Alfred Paper Boy does not know what happened</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="246" start="701.76001" end="703.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy reluctantly drops the subject of Earn's school</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred looks away from Earn. Darius holds the blunt (marijuana cigar) up to the light and examines it</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="247" start="703.88" end="709.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn does not trust Darius or take him seriously</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn turns and sits on the couch in the grass facing Alfred Paper Boy. He asks if there is somewhere they can talk about business without Darius around, because he does not know him</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="248" start="709.52002" end="712.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Darius is offended and sad Earn does not know who he is.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius and Alfred Paper Boy respond at the same time. Darius reminds Earn who he is, that they met when Earn first came to the house. Alfred Paper Boy refuses to leave and says they will talk right where they are.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="249" start="712.76001" end="713.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Darius is upset Earn does not know who he is</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius reminds Earn who he is</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="250" start="713.56" end="716.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn says he knows who Darius is and tells Alfred Paper Boy he is not asking for money</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="251" start="716.35999" end="718">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy tells Earn he should be asking him for money</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="252" start="718" end="721.08002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn argues that he is not truly homeless</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="253" start="721.08002" end="724.03998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy reminds Earn to not confuse mental illness with homelessness</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy takes another hit of the blunt (marijuana cigar). He tells Earn not to be racist and that homelessness is not the same as being crazy</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="254" start="724.03998" end="728.67999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius interjects that it would not be crazy to use a rat as a phone if it worked, it would actually be smart. Alfred Paper Boy takes another hit of the blunt (marijuana cigar).</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="255" start="728.67999" end="731.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is confused by Darius and thinks he is strange</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn looks at Darius and narrows his eyes. Darius continues, saying there are far more rats than people in New York</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="256" start="731.76001" end="738.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius continues talking about how using rats as phones could work. Alfred Paper Boy continues smoking.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="257" start="738.76001" end="741.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is in disbelief about Darius</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn asks Alfred Paper Boy if Darius is his manager</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="258" start="741.28003" end="744.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy laughs leans back on the couch in the grass and says he does not meed a manager; he is just trying to make money. He passes the blunt (marijuana cigar) to Darius.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="259" start="744.71997" end="748.15997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius takes the blunt (marijuana cigar) . He agrees that Alfred Paper Boy does not need a manager. They both laugh. Alfred Paper Boy picks up his phone.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="260" start="748.15997" end="752.44">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn argues that this is not about rap. He says if they manage their money right, they can leave it for their children.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="261" start="752.44" end="753.67999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius cuts Earn off and says he cannot have children</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="262" start="753.67999" end="755.96002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is taken aback</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn replies that he is sure he will find out why eventually</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="263" start="755.96002" end="759.15997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius asks rhetorically when would be an appropriate time to talk about why he cannot have children.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="264" start="759.15997" end="766.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is taken aback by Darius's comment and replies sarcastically.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn replies that apparently now is the time to talk about it. He then turns to Alfred Paper Boy and argues that he will have difficulty selling his music because he is old, does not have a fan base, is not white, and is not selling sex.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="265" start="766.71997" end="769.67999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy, leaning back on the couch in the grass, scoffs and says he does sell sex. He turns to Darius and tells him to play one of his songs.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="266" start="769.67999" end="772.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius puts the blunt (marijuana cigar) in his mouth, picks up his phone, and starts to play a song.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="267" start="772.35999" end="779.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The three men sit on the couch in the grass. Alfred Paper Boy's song starts playing on Darius's phone. Darius starts moving to the beat.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="268" start="779.71997" end="784.44">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius dances, holding his phone and the blunt (marijuana cigar). Alfred Paper Boy starts rapping along to his song.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="269" start="784.44" end="786.47998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy cuts himself off and starts explain that the song is about a massage that turns into sex. The music stops and Darius puts the phone down. Earn cuts him off and says he understands it.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="270" start="786.47998" end="790">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn starts analyzing Alfred Paper Boy's music and advises him to cut the skits out of his mixtape</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="271" start="790" end="791.20001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius disagrees, saying the skits are different</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="272" start="791.20001" end="792.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy hits the blunt (marijuana cigar) again and agrees with Darius.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="273" start="792.35999" end="793.84003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn replies flippantly that he would still cut the skits out</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="274" start="793.84003" end="796.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is offended and frustrated that Earn does not like his music and is trying to tell him what to do</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy looks at Earn and tells him he is not his manager</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="275" start="796.56" end="798.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy and Darius stand up from the couch in the grass and start to walk away</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="276" start="798.88" end="801.79999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn stands up from the couch and follows after them</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="277" start="801.79999" end="807.32001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn continues trying to argue his case, saying he still has connections that could benefit Alfred Paper Boy. Alfred Paper Boy smokes and passes the blunt (marijuana cigar) to Darius.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="278" start="807.32001" end="812.20001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is annoyed with Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The three walk back toward Alfred Paper Boy's house. Alfred Paper Boy says Earn is acting like he's saving him, when really Alfred Paper Boy would be the one helping Earn by giving him a job. Darius blows smoke above his head and blows</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Earn, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="279" start="812.20001" end="813.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn tells Alfred Paper Boy he is trying to help him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Darius, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="280" start="813.28003" end="820.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is angry at Earn and thinks he is selfish</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy turns around and gets in Earn's face. He accuses him of only caring about him when he wants to get rich, and tells him to leave.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="281" start="820.12" end="823.15997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn realizes Alfred Paper Boy made a good point</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn stands motionless and stares after Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="282" start="823.15997" end="824">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">BLACK SCREEN 3</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="283" start="824" end="830.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave, a young white male wearing a lanyard, opens the door and gets out of his car. Earn walks through the parking lot toward Dave.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="284" start="830.56" end="832.40002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave takes drinks out of his car and puts them on the roof. Earn greets Dave.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="285" start="832.40002" end="836.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn and Dave know each other from somewhere in the past</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave recognizes earn and greets him. The two shake hands and hug briefly."</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="286" start="836.52002" end="838.15997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave looks over his shoulder, points, and asks Earn if he just came from a dumpster nearby.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="287" start="838.15997" end="840.08002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn finds the question weird but brushes it off quickly.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn says he was not behind the dumpster and asks Dave how he is doing.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="288" start="840.08002" end="843.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says he did not know Earn was in town. Earn says he has been staying quiet and not getting out much.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="289" start="843.28003" end="846.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says he would've invited Earn to a party if he had known he was in town."</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="290" start="846.52002" end="850.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is not interested in what Dave is saying, but Dave will not stop talking, so Earn pretends to be interested and waits for him to finish.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave continues talking and says the party needed a real DJ. Earn listens patiently.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="291" start="850.12" end="853.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The two stand in the parking lot while Dave continues talking about the DJ at the party</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="292" start="853.76001" end="854.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is pretending to be interested in Dave's story.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn grins and replies.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="293" start="854.56" end="855.91998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn continues pretending to be interested</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave keeps talking about the DJ.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="294" start="855.91998" end="858.84003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave casually uses the "n-word" despite being white, and despite speaking to a black person</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says that he pulled the DJ aside to talk to him</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="295" start="858.84003" end="861.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn awkwardly laughs and casually asks if Dave said that, but is internally taken aback and surprised he said "nigga," especially around him</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn asks if Dave really said that</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="296" start="861.28003" end="862.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave does not understand Earns question because he does not see anything wrong with him saying the n-word ("nigga"), either at all or in conversation with Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says he had tell the DJ that</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="297" start="862.23999" end="865.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is surprised and taken aback that Dave would say the n-word ("nigga") and think it was okay for him to use or say to Earn. He uncomfortably replies, then quickly changes the subject</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn pauses, then changes to subject and asks if Dave has heard of Paper Boy</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="298" start="865.35999" end="868.67999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave seems to reference "the streets" as separate from other listeners or people</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says he has heard Paper Boy and that the streets love it.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="299" start="868.67999" end="869.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn tries to convince Dave to play the song.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn tells Dave he should play Paper Boy on the radio.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="300" start="869.56" end="871.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave says he should play Alfred Paper Boy's song but makes no promises to do so.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave agrees with Earn.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="301" start="871.23999" end="874.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn repeats his suggestion that Dave play Paper Boy on the radio</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="302" start="874.76001" end="876.96002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave replies that KP, the radio station owner, determines what music is played. Dave turns to his car and grabs the drinks on the roof.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="303" start="876.96002" end="878">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave starts to walk away. Earn tells Dave to show KP the song and ask him to play it.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="304" start="878" end="881.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave is suggesting Earn bribe him to play the song</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says KP will play a song if someone pays him upfront.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="305" start="881.28003" end="882.47998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn walks after Dave. Earn asks how much money Dave and KP want to play Paper Boy's song.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="306" start="882.47998" end="883.59998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave is asking for a bribe to do Earn a favor</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave tells him KP would want five hundred dollars to play the song.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="307" start="883.59998" end="886.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is surprised Dave wants so much money.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn and Dave walk toward the radio station. Earn questions the high price.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="308" start="886.76001" end="887.96002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn and Dave walk through the parking lot, Dave carrying the drinks. Dave waves to people he knows and says that connections are important.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="309" start="887.96002" end="889">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn asks Dave to introduce him to his boss, KP.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="310" start="889" end="892">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave is being sarcastic.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave looks at Earn and says he will introduce every person in the city who makes music to his boss.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="311" start="892" end="893.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn argues he is not just some random person with a mixtape, he is Dave's friend.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="312" start="893.12" end="895">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">To Dave, there is nothing special about Earn.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave turns around to look at Earn and tells him he is basically every person who asks for this.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="313" start="895" end="903.91998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn says he does not have five hundred dollars to pay Dave because of his situation with work, rent, and parents. He compares his situation to a drug commercial, except not funny.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="314" start="903.91998" end="907.40002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is again caught off guard by Dave's casual use of racist language despite being white and despite talking to a black person</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave responds that he is getting Earn a good price, and that it usually costs one thousand dollars. He again uses the n-word ("nigga"), casually.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="315" start="907.40002" end="911">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn does not believe KP wants the money, he thinks Dave is trying to make money off of him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn pointedly asks why he is lucky and gets a discount, and how this deal benefits Dave</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="316" start="911" end="913.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave denies taking any money for himself</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="317" start="913.76001" end="916.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says he will pass the money onto KP for Earn. Earn stares at him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="318" start="916.52002" end="920.20001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave is being condescending, and possibly taunting Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says it's fine that Earn cannot pay to have Paper Boy's song played. He says Earn should stay out of the gross music business.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="319" start="920.20001" end="922.84003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn stares at Dave silently. Dave starts to say goodbye and leave</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="320" start="922.84003" end="928.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is still confused by his strange interaction with Dave</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave says he's taking over for another DJ, Speedy, that night. He reaches out his fist to Earn, then turns and walks away. Three black men walk out of the radio station behind Dave. Earn awkwardly, silently raises his arm and fist to Dave.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="321" start="928.35999" end="933.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave conspicuously does not use the n-word ("nigga") with the three men he greets, instead calling them "dude" and "bro"</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave walks toward the building, and greets and shakes hands with the three men walking out. Earn watches him. A custodian pushing a garbage dumpster walks past.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave, Earn, Prince the Janitor</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="322" start="933.12" end="934.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The gets the attention of the custodian pushing the garbage dumpster, and he stops</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Prince the Janitor</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="323" start="934.76001" end="937.79999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn notices Dave does not use racist language with other black people, and wonders if it is just with him</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn asks Prince if Dave ever uses the n-word ("nigga") with him around.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="324" start="937.79999" end="942.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn and Prince have no problem using the n-word ("nigga") with each other, but Prince would never accept a white man using it toward him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Prince looks from over from the garbage dumpster at Dave walking in the door, then back at Earn. He says Dave does not use that language around him, and if he did, he'd beat him up.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Prince the Janitor, Dave</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="325" start="942.35999" end="946.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn's suspicion that Dave only uses that language with him is confirmed</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn walks toward Prince and the garbage dumpster, and asks Prince his name</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="326" start="946.35999" end="947.67999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Prince and Earn seem to get along well, immediately</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Prince tells Earn his name</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Prince the Janitor</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="327" start="947.67999" end="948.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Prince and Earn seem to get along well, immediately.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Prince the Janitor and Earn shake hands. Earn asks if that is really his name.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Prince the Janitor</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="328" start="948.71997" end="949.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Prince and Earn seem to get along well, immediately</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn and Prince the Janitor shake hands. Prince the Janitor says that really is his name.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Prince the Janitor</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="329" start="949.52002" end="952">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is hatching a plan to get into the radio station</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn asks Prince how late he is working at the radio station that night</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Prince the Janitor</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="330" start="952" end="956.40002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's mother plays with Lottie outside Earn's parents' house on the front lawn. Earn's father walks out the front door, holding a drink. Loud rap music plays in the background.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Mom, Dad, Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="331" start="956.40002" end="964.03998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn's father recognizes the people in the car.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">A white car pulls into the driveway as Earn's mother plays with Lottie. The loud music is coming from the car. Earn's father laughs and walks over to the car.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Mom, Dad, Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="332" start="964.03998" end="965.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy and Darius are sitting in the car. Alfred Paper Boy opens the door, gets out, and greets Earn's father (his uncle).</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="333" start="965.71997" end="967.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn's father is happy to see Alfred Paper Boy, and acts much nicer toward him than he does toward Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father walks toward the car and greets Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="334" start="967.12" end="969.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy responds to Earn's father and greets Earn's mother, his aunt.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="335" start="969.56" end="971.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's mother picks up Lottie. Alfred Paper Boy greets Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Mom, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="336" start="971.23999" end="974.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy asks Earn's mother to bring Lottie over to him so he can say hi. She refuses.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="337" start="974.12" end="976.20001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's mother says she will not bring Lottie closer because she can smell the marijuana on Alfred Paper Boy and his car</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Mom, Lottie, Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="338" start="976.20001" end="980.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy playfully denies that the smell is marijuana and says it is the new leather in his car.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="339" start="980.71997" end="982.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's mother does not believe Alfred Paper Boy and retorts</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Mom, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="340" start="982.28003" end="983.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is slightly offended.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy asks what Earn's mother said.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="341" start="983.12" end="983.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father greets Darius.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="342" start="983.64001" end="985.59998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy tells Earn's father that his wife is weird.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy, Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="343" start="985.59998" end="992.52002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius introduces himself to Earn's father and asks if he can measure their tree.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="344" start="992.52002" end="994.03998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Darius stares out of the car at the tree</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="345" start="994.03998" end="999.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn's father is confused by Darius's question</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father stares at Darius, looks at Alfred Paper Boy, looks back at his wife, looks at the tree, and finally says Darius cannot measure it right now.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad, Darius</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="346" start="999.12" end="1003.03998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Darius feels sad and dejected that he cannot measure the tree</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy looks at Darius. Darius sits back in the car and says that answer basically means no. Alfred Paper Boy looks up at Earn's father.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Darius, Alfred Paper Boy, Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="347" start="1003.03998" end="1005.08002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn's father is still confused and taken aback by Darius</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy looks at Earn's father and says he has a question. Earn's father looks up at Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="348" start="1005.08002" end="1008.56">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy tells Earn's father that Earn wants to manage him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="349" start="1008.56" end="1010.12">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn's father is surprised</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father asks "really?". Alfred Paper Boy laughs.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="350" start="1010.12" end="1012.47998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy says he does not trust Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="351" start="1012.47998" end="1013.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Neither man thinks Earn is trustworthy. Earn must have done something in the past to lose their trust.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father says he understands.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad, Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="352" start="1013.64001" end="1014.59998">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Neither man thinks Earn is trustworthy. Earn must have done something in the past to break their trust.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy says it is wrong that he feels he cannot trust Earn.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="353" start="1014.59998" end="1019.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy tells Earn's father he does not feel like he knows Earn anymore. On screen, Earn digs through a shoebox in a bag. He pulls a wad of bills out of a shoe.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="354" start="1019.76001" end="1021.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy asks Earn's father about Earn leaving college at Princeton. Meanwhile, Earn walks into the radio station.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="355" start="1021.71997" end="1026.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father says he never asked about Princeton, and that Earn would tell Alfred Paper Boy before him. Meanwhile, Earn walks into the radio station.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="356" start="1026.28003" end="1030.68005">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Alfred Paper Boy says Earn is good at keeping his mouth shut. Meanwhile, Prince, the radio station custodian, unlocks the door to the radio booth and lets Earn inside.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Prince the Janitor</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="357" start="1030.68005" end="1033.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave is in the radio booth, speaking into a mic while music plays on the radio</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="358" start="1033.76001" end="1036.35999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn walks up to the booth and taps on the glass with the CD and money</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="359" start="1036.35999" end="1038.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave motions for Earn to come inside and give him the money.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="360" start="1038.28003" end="1040.40002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn knows Dave would keep the money for himself and is not going to give it to him. Earn taunts Dave with the money.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn does not give the money to Dave, but instead looks at him and walks past.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Dave</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="361" start="1040.40002" end="1042.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Dave is surprised and taken aback that Earn is giving the money to KP instead</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Dave looks at Earn as he walks away</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dave</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="362" start="1042.76001" end="1051.95996">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn knows Dave would keep the money for himself, and gives it to KP instead</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn walks up to a door that says Kyle P. and slips an envelope with the CD and money under the door.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="363" start="1051.95996" end="1053.92004">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father tells Alfred Paper Boy that Earn is trying like everyone else. Meanwhile, Earn stands up and looks at the sign that says "Kyle P."</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="364" start="1053.92004" end="1057.71997">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn's father may not particularly respect Earn, but he has faith in him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Back at Earn's parents' house, his father tells Alfred Paper Boy Earn gets things done when he wants to.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Dad, Alfred</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="365" start="1057.71997" end="1061.40002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Alfred Paper Boy is convinced Earn would be a good manager.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn's father says Earn does things on his terms. Alfred Paper Boy nods.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Alfred Paper Boy</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="366" start="1061.40002" end="1064.95996">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn sits on a bus, holding his sleeping daughter, Lottie. Earn and Lottie are both wearing headphones, listening to music. Earn looks down at Lottie.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="367" start="1064.95996" end="1070.95996">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn looks up from his sleeping daughter, Lottie, and then looks at the man across the aisle.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="368" start="1070.95996" end="1074.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">The man</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">A bald, black man in a suit sits across from Earn. He tells Earn that his mind is racing.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="369" start="1074.76001" end="1077.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The strange man looks at Earn and speaks</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="370" start="1077.64001" end="1083.56006">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn looks at the strange man. The strange man walks over and sits down next to Earn.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
        <attribute name="Music Presence">true</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="371" start="1083.56006" end="1088.40002">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is at first annoyed the stranger is trying to talk to him</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn takes off his headphones and looks at the stranger. Earn rolls his eyes.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="372" start="1088.40002" end="1093.56006">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn opens up to the stranger</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The stranger pulls a jar of Nutella out of his pocket and unscrews the lid. Earn looks at him and says he feels like he always loses.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man, Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="373" start="1093.56006" end="1100.19995">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn feels like the universe is against him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn wonders if some people are just meant to always lose so that others can win.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="374" start="1100.19995" end="1104.07996">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn feels it is his purpose to be a perpetual loser.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn wonders if his constant bad luck is the universe balancing itself for others' good luck</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="375" start="1104.07996" end="1107.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn continues wondering aloud to the stranger about his luck and balance. The stranger spreads Nutella on bread with a plastic knife to make a sandwich.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="376" start="1107.64001" end="1112.80005">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn wonders aloud if his purpose is to make life easier for people who win as much as he loses. The stranger continues spreading Nutella on bread to make a sandwich.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="377" start="1112.80005" end="1116.80005">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn finishes speaking and reaches down to touch Lottie's hand. The stranger finishes spreading the Nutella on the bread and puts the knife down.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man, Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="378" start="1116.80005" end="1121.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn looks down at Lottie. The stranger puts the two pieces of bread together to make a sandwich and begins to explain to Earn the nature of life, struggle, and resistance. Earn turns to look at the stranger</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man, Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="379" start="1121.64001" end="1125.64001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is curious about who the strange man is</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn looks sideways at the stranger and narrows his eyes. The stranger continues speaking about resistance and the way things are.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="380" start="1125.64001" end="1131.56006">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The stranger tells Earn that victory is ignoring failure</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="381" start="1131.56006" end="1136.28003">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The stranger essentially tells Earn to go with the flow and let events guide him.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="382" start="1136.28003" end="1141.95996">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn misunderstands the stranger, and thinks the man is giving him advice on how to pick up women</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn politely tells the stranger he does not need that advice, thanks him, and turns away.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="383" start="1141.95996" end="1144.68005">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn nods and turns away from the stranger to look at his daughter, Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="384" start="1144.68005" end="1147.76001">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The stranger turns and reaches toward Earn, holding the sandwich, and tells him to bite it</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="385" start="1147.76001" end="1149.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is confused by the stranger's request</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn turns and looks at the sandwich</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="386" start="1149.23999" end="1153.80005">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is confused, puzzled</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn turns down the stranger's request to bite the sandwich</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie, Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="387" start="1153.80005" end="1157.80005">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The stranger pressures Earn and insists he bite the sandwich</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="388" start="1157.80005" end="1162.92004">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">A police car drives past the bus with its lights flashing and siren on. Earn turns to look at the police car, then looks down at Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man, Earn</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="389" start="1162.92004" end="1166.04004">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn turns back to look at the stranger, but he is gone. The jar of Nutella is still sitting on the empty seat.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="390" start="1166.04004" end="1168.80005">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn sits up and looks out the window of the bus.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="391" start="1168.80005" end="1173.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">The dog with the stranger is the dog from the opening scene</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">The stranger walks off into the woods, followed by a dog</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Strange Man</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="392" start="1173.88" end="1176">
        <attribute name="narrative details - internal">Earn is confused by the interaction with the stranger.</attribute>
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn sits back on his seat, holding Lottie.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="393" start="1176" end="1181.31995">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn looks down at his sleeping daughter</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="394" start="1181.31995" end="1189.88">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn gently pulls Lottie's headphones off and picks up his phones.</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="395" start="1189.88" end="1194.23999">
        <attribute name="narrative details - external">Earn types on his phone while holding Lottie</attribute>
        <attribute name="characters on screen">Earn, Lottie</attribute>
      </el>
      <el index="396" start="1194.23999" end="1199.28003">
